@startuml product-list-flow
title Product search and shopping list creation
autonumber

actor "User" as User
participant "Web React\nNewShoppingList" as Web
participant "API Laravel\nProductController" as API
participant "IndexProductAction" as IndexAction
participant "ProductRepository" as ProductRepo
participant "MeilisearchProductSearch" as Search
database "MySQL" as MySQL
participant "ListController / StoreListAction" as ListAPI
participant "ListRepository" as ListRepo

== Search from the new list page ==
User -> Web: Enters a search term
Web -> Web: Waits 500 ms, then calls fetchProducts
alt Search HTTP/network request fails
  Web -> API: GET /api/products?search={term}&page=1\nAuthorization: Bearer token
  API --> Web: HTTP error or network failure
  Web -> Web: fetchProducts catches error and sets productsError
  Web --> User: “Could not load products. Please try again.”
else Search succeeds
  Web -> API: GET /api/products?search={term}&page=1\nAuthorization: Bearer token
  API -> IndexAction: index(validated request)
  IndexAction -> ProductRepo: paginate(user, filters)
  ProductRepo -> Search: search(ProductSearchCriteria)
  alt Meilisearch is available
    Search -> Search: Runs text search and returns ordered IDs
  else Meilisearch fails
    Search -> MySQL: MySqlProductSearch.search(criteria)
    MySQL --> Search: Ranked IDs; fallbackUsed=true
  end
  ProductRepo -> MySQL: Loads validated products, relations, and page\nfilters by search IDs
  MySQL --> ProductRepo: Products and pagination
  ProductRepo --> IndexAction: Product page
  opt search term is not empty
    IndexAction -> MySQL: Inserts SearchLog (term, engine, duration, fallback)
    MySQL --> IndexAction: Search log persisted
  end
  IndexAction --> API: Paginated products
  API --> Web: 200 JSON: data, meta\nClientProductResource includes name and average_price
  Web --> User: Displays products and prices for selection

  User -> Web: Selects products and enters a list name
  Web -> Web: Keeps selections locally; validates name and items
  Web -> ListAPI: POST /api/lists\n{name, products:[{product:{id}, quantity}]}\nAuthorization: Bearer token
  ListAPI -> ListAPI: ListStoreRequest validates name, items, and existing IDs
  alt Invalid data / product no longer exists
    ListAPI --> Web: 422 JSON with message and errors
    Web -> Web: saveList catches error; does not navigate to /
    note right of Web
      Current code logs the error to the console;
      this page does not show a dedicated error message.
    end note
  else Data is valid
    ListAPI -> ListRepo: DB::transaction: createForUser(user, data)
    ListRepo -> MySQL: INSERT list (user_id, name, total=0)
    MySQL --> ListRepo: List created
    ListAPI -> ListRepo: attachProducts(list, IDs and quantities)
    ListRepo -> MySQL: INSERT list-product relations
    MySQL --> ListRepo: Relations persisted
    ListAPI -> ProductRepo: incrementListAdded(product IDs)
    ProductRepo -> MySQL: Increments listAdded for products
    MySQL --> ProductRepo: Update completed
    ListAPI --> Web: 200 JSON: “List created successfully!” + ClientListResource
    Web -> Web: navigate("/")
    Web --> User: Returns to the home page after saving
  end
end

note over Search,MySQL
  Meilisearch is an optional search index; failures fall back to MySQL.
  The list and its relations are written to MySQL in a transaction.
end note
@enduml
